{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01024",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 6.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.1,
      "end_seconds": 11.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.06,
      "end_seconds": 25.21,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Yeah, it's my face drooping on one side. I don't know what's causing it. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 26.86,
      "end_seconds": 36.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse 88, temp 36.9 degrees, blood pressure 168 over 89."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.1,
      "end_seconds": 38.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.4,
      "end_seconds": 51.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.82,
      "end_seconds": 58.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "I'd say two days. Actually, no, closer to about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.81,
      "end_seconds": 63.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "I was just gonna say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 64.07,
      "end_seconds": 71.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.16,
      "end_seconds": 75.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "alright, later, thanks please go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.01,
      "end_seconds": 88.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.0,
      "text": "As for sudden headache, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.32,
      "end_seconds": 91.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.19,
      "end_seconds": 99.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "honestly, once or twice a day oh, um, and and weakness in my right arm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.54,
      "end_seconds": 107.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.41,
      "end_seconds": 115.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.05,
      "end_seconds": 125.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.95,
      "end_seconds": 135.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "About a eight out of ten. Oh, and slurred speech. That's been about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.46,
      "end_seconds": 144.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Have you had your face drooping on one side before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.71,
      "end_seconds": 149.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last year it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.35,
      "end_seconds": 154.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Have you had fever, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.27,
      "end_seconds": 156.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.66,
      "end_seconds": 162.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Have you noticed seizure or loss of consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.04,
      "end_seconds": 167.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Um, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.22,
      "end_seconds": 172.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.99,
      "end_seconds": 174.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.23,
      "end_seconds": 178.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.73,
      "end_seconds": 183.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.15,
      "end_seconds": 186.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.47,
      "end_seconds": 196.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "It's, It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.42,
      "end_seconds": 200.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.04,
      "end_seconds": 216.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "For the heart rhythm, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 217.74,
      "end_seconds": 222.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.07,
      "end_seconds": 228.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.41,
      "end_seconds": 232.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "not with me i'll bring it next time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.99,
      "end_seconds": 254.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.29,
      "end_seconds": 258.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.89,
      "end_seconds": 262.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.22,
      "end_seconds": 268.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.04,
      "end_seconds": 270.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.15,
      "end_seconds": 279.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat is known to us, good to have that clear. Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.49,
      "end_seconds": 287.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Okay, so I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.56,
      "end_seconds": 293.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "So, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.08,
      "end_seconds": 305.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a reaction to naproxen when I was younger, stomach pain, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.6,
      "end_seconds": 308.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.95,
      "end_seconds": 310.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.65,
      "end_seconds": 316.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.75,
      "end_seconds": 330.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Your right face droops, your right arm is weak and your speech is slurred."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.49,
      "end_seconds": 350.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.78,
      "text": "so, all finished, thank you. So where does that leave us? My working impression is a possible stroke, within the treatment window. I'd also keep a migraine with aura in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 351.06,
      "end_seconds": 355.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I've already done a blood sugar test, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.6,
      "end_seconds": 364.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "okay, I'll take a look at that we should do an urgent CT scan of the head for possible stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 365.89,
      "end_seconds": 369.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I can book that for Friday at 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.02,
      "end_seconds": 393.04,
      "duration_seconds": 22.02,
      "text": "call an ambulance now, you need hospital immediately. I'm going to send a referral to the stroke team. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's review you straight away. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.26,
      "end_seconds": 398.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.74,
      "end_seconds": 401.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "look after yourself"
    }
  ]
}